   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What is not needed",
     "texto": [
      "To say that something does not need to be done, use **-(으)ㄹ 필요가 없다**: 가다 → **갈 필요가 없어요** (there is no need to go), 기다리다 → **기다릴 필요가 없어요** (there is no need to wait).",
      "다시 올 **필요가 없어요** = there is no need to come back."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What is needed",
     "texto": [
      "To say that something is needed: **-(으)ㄹ 필요가 있다**.",
      "설명할 **필요가 있어요** = it is necessary to explain it."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "No need and it is enough to",
     "texto": [
      "**-(으)ㄹ 필요가 없다** says that an action is not necessary. By contrast, **-(으)면 되다** indicates that it is enough to meet a condition: 확인하면 돼요 = it is enough to check it. They do not mean the same thing."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
